{
  "name": "simplesched",
  "description": "simplesched is a lightweight coroutine scheduler for Rust that provides a cooperative multitasking environment with integrated asynchronous I/O. It implements an M:N threading model using a global lock-free task queue and a set of worker threads that multiplex coroutines onto OS threads. The library abstracts mio to provide synchronous-looking networking primitives for TCP, UDP, and HTTP, enabling a Go-like programming style for high-concurrency systems.",
